{"id":"word:hebrew:H2421","type":"word","title":"חָיָה","subtitle":"H2421 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to live , whether literally or figuratively; causatively, to revive","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָיָה (H2421) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 265 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָיָה (châyâh) means to live , whether literally or figuratively; causatively, to revive First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָיָה","transliteration":"châyâh","pronunciation":"khaw-yaw'","strong":"H2421","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2421","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַֽ/יְחִי","וַ/יְחִ֣י","וַֽ/יְחִ֣י","יְחִ֥י","חַיֵּֽ/נִי"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3ms",43],["HVqi3ms",30],["HVqa",11],["HVqj3ms",10],["HC/Vqq3ms",9],["HVpv2ms/Sp1cs",9],["HVqi2ms",8],["HC/Vqv2mp",8],["HVpi3ms",7],["HVqi3mp",7]]},"definitions":{"short":"to live , whether literally or figuratively; causatively, to revive","usage":"keep (leave, make) alive, × certainly, give (promise) life, (let, suffer to) live, nourish up, preserve (alive), quicken, recover, repair, restore (to life), revive, (× God) save (alive, life, lives), × surely, be whole.","full":"H2421. chayah I. חוה (Phoenician חוא live = Hebrew חָיָה q. v.) חָיָה 283 verb live (Late Hebrew Phoenician id. ; Arabic , ; Sabean חיו Mordt ZMG 1876, 28 ; Ethiopic Aramaic , חֲיָא ; Palmyrene חיי life, life-time , Vog 32, 74 ) — Qal 203 Perfect חָיָה Eccl 6:6 4 t.; יְ֯חָיָה Jer 21:9 ; 38:2 ; חַי Gen 5:5 23 t. (this and the following form are treated as עע֞ , the original weakness of the stem final י admitting of either לה֞ or עע֞ , Ges § 76 (2) g); וְחֵי Lev 25:36 (Bö § 1181 ); 3 feminine singular חָֽיְתָה Gen 12:13 ; Jer 38:17 ; וָחָ֑יָה Exod 1:16 (for חַיָּה Bö § 1123 (3), Samaritan חיתה ); 2 masculine singular חָיִיתָ Deut 30:16 , חָיִתָה Jer 38:17 ; 3 masculine plural חָיוּ Num 14:38 , וְחָיוּ consecutive 4:19 + Zech 10:9 (where read Pi`el וְחִיּוּ Sta ZAW i. 1881, 22 so ᵐ5 ); וִחְיִיתֶם Ezek 37:5 2 t.; Imperfect יִחְיֶה Gen 17:18 27 t.; יְחִי Deut 33:6 10 t.; וִיחִי Psa 49:10 2 t.; וְיֶחִ֑י Isa 38:21 , וַיְחִי Gen 5:3 37t.; וַיֶּחִ֑י Deut 4:33 4 t.; 3 feminine singular תִּחְיֶה Josh 6:17 , תְּחִי Gen 19:20 5 t.; 2 masculine singular תִּחְיֶה 27:40 7 t.; 2 feminine singular תִּחְיִי 2Kin 4:7 ; 1 singular אֶחְיֶה 1:2 8 t.; 3 masculine plural יִחְיוּ Josh 9:21 8 t.; 3 feminine plural תִּחְיֶינָה Ezek 13:19 ; 37:3 ; 2 masculine plural תִּחְיוּ Deut 4:1-2 t.; תִּחְיוּן 5:30 ; 8:1 ; 1 plural נִחְיֶה 2Kin 7:4 7 t.; Imperative וֶחְיֵה Gen 20:7 ; Prov 4:4 , וֶחְיֶ֯ה 7:2 ; feminine singular חֲיִי Ezek 16:6 (twice in verse); masculine plural וִחְיוּ Gen 42:18 7 t.; Infinitive absolute חָיֹה 2Kin 8:10 6 t.; חָיוֺ Ezek 3:21 3 t.; construct לִחְיוֺת 33:12 , suffix חֲיוֺתָם Josh 5:8 ; &#8212; 1 live: a. have life , Gen 31:32 (E), Exod 33:20 (J), Num 4:19 (P), Deut 30:16 +; also in phrase וַיְחִי and he lived (so many years) with accusative of time, Gen 5:3-30 (16 t.) 9:28 ; 11:11-26 (14 t.) 47:28 (all P), 50:22 (E), 2Kin 14:17 2Chr 25:25 ; Job 42:16 . b. continue in life, remain alive Gen 20:7 (E), Lev 25:36 ; 2Sam 12:22 +; also ׳ח נפשׁ live, of the soul or the self Gen 12:13 ; 19:20 (J), 1Kin 20:32 ; Psa 119:175 ; Jer 38:2 , 17 , 20 ; Isa 55:3 ; הַיָּ֑לֶד וְחַי and the boy may live 2Sam 12:22 ; ׳ח לִפְנֵי live in the presence of Gen 17:18 (P) Hosea 6:2 ; ׳ח ׳ב live among Lam 4:20 . c. sustain life, live on or upon ( על ), of the animal life, by the sword Gen 27:40 (J), by bread Deut 8:3 ; elsewhere in pregnant sense of fulness of life in divine favour, sustained by ( על ) everything that issueth out of the mouth of ׳י 8:3 ; his promises (?) Isa 38:16 ; of wicked man, by repentance Ezek 33:19 ; with בְּ by the statutes and judgments of ׳י if a man do them, Lev 18:5 (H) Ezek 20:11 , 13 , 21 , 25 ; Neh 9:29 ; יִחְיֶה בֶּאֱמוּנָתוֺ צַדִּיק a righteous man by his faithfulness shall live Hab 2:4 . d. live (prosperously) הַמֶּלֶך יְחִי may the king live 1Sam 10:24 ; 2Sam 16:16 (twice in verse); 1Kin 1:25 , 31 , 34 , 39 ; 2Kin 11:12 ; 2Chr 23:11 ; לְבַבְכֶם יְחִי Psa 22:27 ; 69:33 ; יחיה לעולם המלך Neh 2:3 . 2 be quickened, revive: a. from sickness Num 21:8-9 , Josh 5:8 (E) 2Kin 1:2 ; 8:8-9 , 10 , 14 ; 20:1 , 7 = Isa 38:1 ; 38:9 ; 38:21 . b. from discouragement of the spirit Gen 45:27 (E). c. from faintness Judg 15:19 . d. from death 2Kin 13:21 ; Job 14:14 ; Isa 26:14 , 19 ; by return of נפשׁ 1Kin 17:22 , of רוּהַ Ezek 37:3 , 5 , 6 , 9 , 10 , 14 (and so Judg 15:19 c ). Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular חִיָּה Psa 22:30 ; 3 feminine singular suffix חִיָּ֑תְנִי 119:50 ; 2 masculine singular suffix חִיִּיתַנִי 30:4 ; חִיִּיתָ֑נִי Paslm 119:93 ; 3 plural חִיּוּ Judg 21:14 , הַחִיִּיתֶם Num 31:15 ; Imperfect יְחַיֶּה 1Sam 27:9 +, etc.; Imperative suffix חַיֵּנִי Psa 119:25 8 t., חַיֵּיהוּ Hab 3:2 ; Infinitive construct חַיּוֺת Gen 7:3 ; Ezek 13:19 ; suffix חַיֹּתֵנוּ Deut 6:24 +, etc.; Participle מְחַיֶּה Neh 9:6 ; 1Sam 2:6 ; &#8212; 1 preserve alive, let live Exod 1:17-18 , 22 ; 22:17 ; Josh 9:15 (JE), Gen 12:12 (J), Num 31:15 (P), Deut 6:24 ; 20:16 ; Judg 21:14 ; 1Sam 27:9 , 11 ; 1Kin 18:5 ; 2Kin 7:4 ; Jer 49:11 ; Ezek 3:18 ; Hab 3:2 ; Job 36:6 ; Psa 30:4 ; 33:19 ; 41:3 ; 138:7 ; ׳ח נפשׁ preserve oneself alive 22:30 ; Ezek 18:27 , or preserve persons alive 13:18-19 , or preserve life 1Kin 20:31 ; ׳ח זרע preserve seed alive Gen 7:3 ; 19:32 , 34 (J); keep in existence heaven and earth Neh 9:6 ; nourish , young cow Isa 7:21 , lamb 2Sam 12:3 . 2 give life , to man when created Job 33:4 . 3 quicken, revive, refresh: a. restore to life , the dead 1Sam 2:6 ; Deut 32:39 ; Hosea 6:2 ; the dying Psa 71:20 . b. cause to grow , grain Hosea 14:8 . c. restore , a ruined city 1Chr 11:8 , stones destroyed by fire Nehemiah 3:34. d. revive , the people of ׳י by ׳י himself with fulness of life in his favour Psa 80:19 ; 85:7 ; 119:25 , 37 , 40 , 50 , 88 , 93 , 107 , 149 , 154 , 156 , 159; 143:11 ; Eccl 7:12 . Hiph`il Perfect הֶחֱיָה Josh 6:25 5 t.; 2 masculine singular suffix הֶחֱיִתָנוּ Gen 47:25 ; 1 singular הֶחֱיֵיתִי Num 22:33 , הַחֲיִתֶם Josh 2:13 ; Judg 8:19 ; Imperative suffix הַחֲיֵינִי Isa 38:16 ; הַחֲיוּ Num 31:18 ; Infinitive absolute הַחֲיֵה Josh 9:20 ; construct הַחֲיוֺת Gen 6:20 6 t.; הַחֲיֹת 6:19 ; 50:20 ; suffix הַחֲיֹתוֺ Ezek 13:22 ; &#8212; 1 preserve alive, let live Gen 45:7 ; 50:20 (E), 47:25 ; Num 22:33 ; Josh 2:13 ; 6:25 (all J), 14:10 (D); Gen 6:19-20 , Num 31:18 ; Josh 9:20 (P), Judg 8:19 ; 2Sam 8:2 ; Ezek 13:22 ; with נפשׁ Gen 19:19 (J). 2 quicken, revive: a. restore to health, a leper 2Kin 5:7 , Hezekiah Isa 38:16 . b. revive the לֵב and רוּחַ Isa 57:15 (twice in verse). c. restore to life , the dead 2Kin 8:1 , 5 (3 t. in verse).","rootNote":"a primitive root (compare 2331 , 2421 );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 8","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 8","1Kgs 1 25","1Kgs 1 31","1Kgs 1 34","1Kgs 1 39","1Kgs 17 22","1Kgs 18 5","1Kgs 20 31"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":265,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְחַיֶּ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpi3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 25","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְחִ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqj3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 31","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְחִ֗י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqj3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 34","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְחִ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqj3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 39","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יְחִ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqj3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 22","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יֶּֽ